WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.260
In 1792, Mary Wollstonecraft argued that
women are rational beings who deserve

2
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.530
the same education and rights as men.

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:15.130
In 1979, the United Nations agreed a
convention often called an international

4
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.110
bill of rights for women.

5
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.240
Yet some practices that harm
girls, like female genital cutting,

6
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.980
are still defended as
tradition, even as faith.

7
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.330
So when a practice is
defended as culture or faith,

8
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.200
who decides whether it wrongs women?

9
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:36.120
In this mission, you'll read Bible texts
that Christians use both for equal dignity

10
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.990
and for different roles.

11
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.150
Then you'll map feminist views, and test
the claim that religion is a barrier.

12
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.900
Your mission: weigh up who should decide
whether a practice defended as culture

13
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.790
or faith wrongs women.
